Explanation of the change:

- We pull `vertical` out of the incoming props so it’s no longer blindly spread onto the `<ul>` (and so that React doesn’t warn about an unknown DOM attribute).
- We add the `${prefix}--progress--vertical` class when `vertical` is true.  That ensures you get the same vertical‐mode flex-alignment rules in the skeleton state that the normal `ProgressIndicator` already has.
